From 7960f24d013131c617309c7d598c6817fef81d0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:07:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] feat(live): fast voice pass with picker confirmation in
 the live loop

Live MVP step 3 (LIVE_CLIPPING off). The full reaction picker costs ~100 s
per 120 s window on CPU, almost all facecam analysis; voice evidence costs
~5 s. live/voice_scan.py runs extract_voice_evidence on only the audio
recorded since the last tick, flags onsets with the picker's own rules
(two voice signals z>=3, strong laugh, scream rule), causal baselines, and
confirm_with_picker() runs the full picker on +/-15 s around a flag.

Measured on the Kai sample played as live: flags at 31 s / 34 s (laugh,
vocal); confirmation still ~75-80 s per call (fixed per-call cost, not
window length) so flags queue; an audio-led candidate had its preview 46 s
after the moment while live. Open items in handoff/live-mvp/STATUS.md
(confirmation latency, voice-pass recall, one confirmed reaction not
reaching the candidate list).
Tests: test_live_voice_scan 3/3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
